{{ ref: 7e5fc74b-6251-45d2-a560-1d024ad02a33 }}
- **Surface Area**: `crates/engine` published as the `strata-engine` crate (`analyze`, `snapshot_from_root`, `load_config`, `AnalyzeConfig`, `AnalyzeResult`, `StrataError`), `crates/cli` as the `strata` binary
--{ ref: 7e5fc74b-6251-45d2-a560-1d024ad02a33 }--
{{ ref: 220235d7-47d4-4169-a5e1-6cb6c99e7fba }}
- **Description**: One engine, two faces (AD-5). The `strata-engine` crate exposes analysis as a pure, deterministic Rust function for CI bots, dashboards, editors, and custom tooling; the CLI (`analyze`, `tree`, `diff`, `violations`, `report`) is a thin shell over the same surface — no logic exists that library consumers cannot reach. There is no HTTP server, no `serve` command, and no network access of any kind.
--{ ref: 220235d7-47d4-4169-a5e1-6cb6c99e7fba }--
