{{ ref: e44e6122-166b-435f-b71e-17cc1fbc27e5 }}
- **Behaviour**: `analyze` is pure — identical snapshot + config + seed returns byte-identical results, so callers cache by `result.snapshot_hash` (blake3). The crate re-exports all `ir` types, so consumers can assemble snapshots from custom adapters and skip the filesystem entirely. All failures are structured `StrataError` variants mirroring the Reference error catalogue; nothing panics across the crate boundary.
--{ ref: e44e6122-166b-435f-b71e-17cc1fbc27e5 }--
{{ ref: f64fa21a-2747-4b44-bf9a-ce1fe446f6b8 }}
- **Compatibility**: Follows semver from 0.1; `AnalyzeResult` grows additively within a minor line. A CLI ↔ library parity test (PI-12) guards against drift between the two surfaces.
--{ ref: f64fa21a-2747-4b44-bf9a-ce1fe446f6b8 }--